  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Pacific Humanitarian Warehouse Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This investment will fund the enhancement of humanitarian warehouses, either through leasing, refurbishment or construction options, and prepositioning of Humanitarian and Emergency Relief Supplies in up to 14 Pacific island countries and Timor-Leste. The program will be delivered over an eight-year period. The investment will be guided by the cross-cutting themes of localisation, gender equality, disability and social inclusion and green humanitarian action. Australia has secured support for approximately half of the program costs for the life of the program. Development partners, through Australian coordination and advocacy, have committed complimentary supporting funding. PHWP is implemented by an integrated team led by The Pacific Community and supported by Infrastructure and logistics specialists.</narrative>
  </description>
